orth Garber Creek, Pine Creek, Coal Creek,\nKinney Creek, West Toll Gate Creek, Willow Creek, Plum Creek,\nAntelope Creek, Bayou Gulch, First Creek, Watson Park Creek, Dry\nGulch, Happy Canyon Creek, Lake Gulch, South Platte River and\nEast Toll Gate Creek. Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1\ninch are expected over the area. This additional rain will result\nin minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nSouthern Aurora, eastern Centennial, Castle Rock, Parker, Lone\nTree, Larkspur, Castle Pines, Franktown, Sedalia, The Pinery,\nPerry Park, Ponderosa Park, Devil's Head, Arapahoe Park,\nFoxfield, Castlewood Canyon and Shamballa.","ends":"2026-07-29T17:45:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Arapahoe, CO; Douglas, CO; Elbert, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.13e662d6e196dc40e2d5e38b16af1442896771da.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.13e662d6e196dc40e2d5e38b16af1442896771da.001.1"},{"event":"Special Weather Statement","headline":"Special Weather Statement issued July 29 at 2:38PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"At 238 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm near\nCastle Pines, or 18 miles south of Denver, moving northeast at 10\nmph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and penny size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nSouthern Aurora, eastern Centennial, eastern Highlands Ranch,\nCastle Rock, Parker, Lone Tree, The Pinery, Castle Pines, Franktown\nand Foxfield.","ends":"2026-07-29T15:15:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"North Douglas County Below 6000 Feet/Denver/West Adams and Arapahoe Counties/East Broomfield County; Elbert/Central and East Douglas Counties Above 6000 Feet","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a731f731a2dc04ede6ba3943d026ba12b26d0f66.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2